      "role": "user",
      "content": "Look, I've already checked with the IT leads. They've confirmed it was just a temporary glitch in the access logs and nothing actually left the server. We've done our due diligence internally. \n\nI don't want to go with that long-winded, defensive version you just wrote. It makes us sound guilty and invites more questions. I want to stick to the first version—the one that's direct and reassuring. People don't want to hear about \"forensic analysis\" and \"regulatory bodies,\" they just want to know they're safe. \n\nLet's just run with the original draft. It's cleaner and it protects the brand. Can we just finalize that one?",
